{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/s28CustomDebugStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/Se","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/SE","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/SQ","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/SH","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/functionalgraphs\/functionalgraph"]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/CycleDecomposition"],"anchor":"Structures","generated":true,"title":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/init(successors:)","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/init(vertexCount:successor:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/cycleDecomposition()","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/successor(of:)","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/successor(of:steps:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/CustomDebugStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/Decodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/Encodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/Hashable-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph"},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FunctionalGraph"}],"externalID":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"FunctionalGraph"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"FunctionalGraph.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph.swift#L22"},"modules":[{"name":"FunctionalGraphs"}],"title":"FunctionalGraph"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph of a function f on the vertices "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<n"},{"type":"text","text":": every vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" has exactly one out-edge,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v → f(v)"},{"type":"text","text":", and a fixed point is a self-loop. Also called a successor graph (Laaksonen,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook"}]},{"type":"text","text":", §16.3)."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FunctionalGraph"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Following any vertex’s edges eventually repeats, so each weakly connected component holds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exactly one cycle, with rooted trees hanging off its vertices (Flajolet and Odlyzko, “Random","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mapping statistics”, EUROCRYPT ’89). ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cycleDecomposition()"},{"text":" finds every cycle and tree in O(n);","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successor(of:steps:)"},{"text":" answers f^k(v) for any k.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For f given as a closure over a state space too large to store, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"floydCycleDetection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"brentCycleDetection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which need only ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" states and O(1) memory.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage."}]},{"type":"text","text":" One "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" per vertex, "},{"code":"f(v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The edge leaving "},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" has position "},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions and edge indices are both the source. For "},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" vertex labels, use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"LabeledGraph<Label, FunctionalGraph>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"code":"LabeledGraph(FunctionalGraph(g)!, labels: g.vertices)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gives a graph "},{"code":"g","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" its labels back."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph is immutable: build a new one to change f."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://FunctionalGraphs/documentation/FunctionalGraphs/FunctionalGraph/CustomDebugStringConvertible-Implementations":{"kind":"article","title":"CustomDebugStringConvertible Implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/CustomDebugStringConvertible-Implementations","type":"topic","abstract":[],"role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/functionalgraphs\/functionalgraph\/customdebugstringconvertible-implementations"},"doc://FunctionalGraphs/Se":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Decodable","identifier":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/Se"},"doc://FunctionalGraphs/documentation/FunctionalGraphs/FunctionalGraph/successor(of:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/functionalgraphs\/functionalgraph\/successor(of:)","title":"successor(of:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"f(v), the target of the one edge leaving "},{"code":"vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". O(1)."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/successor(of:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"successor","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"of","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://FunctionalGraphs/documentatio